SuiteCRM 8.10.2 tightened User::hasSaveAccess() from `return true` to
`return is_admin($current_user)` for a record without an id, and
restrictAdminOnlyFields() now forces `status = Inactive` on such a record
(release commit 6c7ce002a). CreateUser::create() runs while the browser is
still anonymous, because it is the LDAP and SAML auto-create path
(AppLdapUserProvider::createUser, AppSamlUserFactory::createUser, both via
UserHandler::createExternalAuthUser), so every first login of a directory
account ends in `RuntimeException: Not authorized`, HTTP 500 on POST /login
and no session after a SAML assertion. v8.10.1 and earlier exempted a new
record from both guards; upstream has no release and no hotfix carrying a fix.

\CreateUser is reachable only from that provisioning stack and from the
installer, so the admin context is raised here instead of relaxing the guards,
which keeps them closed for every request-driven save.

Generated with `diff -u` against the v8.10.2 tarball and applied with `-F0`, so
the build fails instead of letting GNU patch's default fuzz factor land the
hunk somewhere upstream moved it to.

